{#-
  Built-in `firing` template (ADR 001 D10).

  Receives one variable, `alert`. Every field of it is always defined and already
  escaped for Slack; see docs/src/how-to/customize-templates.md for the full list.

  Output is Slack `mrkdwn`. The colour bar, the attachment wrapper and the 3000-character
  block limit are applied by the relay around whatever this produces, so a template only
  ever decides wording.
-#}
*:rotating_light: FIRING · {{ alert.alertname }}*{% if alert.severity %} · `{{ alert.severity }}`{% endif %}
{% if alert.summary %}{{ alert.summary }}
{% endif %}
{%- if alert.description and alert.description != alert.summary %}{{ alert.description }}
{% endif %}
{%- for key, value in alert.labels|items %}{% if key != "alertname" and key != "severity" %}`{{ key }}={{ value }}` {% endif %}{% endfor %}

_firing since {{ alert.started_at }} · {{ alert.duration }}_
{%- if alert.runbook_url %} · <{{ alert.runbook_url }}|runbook>{% endif %}
{%- if alert.generator_url %} · <{{ alert.generator_url }}|source>{% endif %}
